      "extract": "Here we shall consider one of the simplest examples of solutions to the WDVV equations coming from Seiberg-Witten theory. These are related to $SU(N+1)$ perturbative prepotentials [@MMM] and the corresponding Riemann surface is degenerate. With $a_{ij}\\equiv a_i-a_j$ the perturbative prepotential is given by $$\\label{pertpre} {\\cal F}= {1\\over 2}\\sum_{i<j}^N a_{ij}^2\\log {a_{ij}\\over\\Lambda} + {1\\over 2}\\sum_{i=1}^N",
