      "extract": "Although the WDVV equations arise in several different physical settings no unifying geometry as yet underpins them. With the additional restrictions of topological field theory Frobenius manifolds successfully encode the geometry, but the restrictions are too severe to allow other interesting examples coming from Seiberg-Witten theory and the dispersionless limits of solutions to the Hirota equations. In this note",
